[{"text": "The assembly will hear an address by his", "start": 1.6, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "excellency Tidoro Nigimo Oang Mangu,", "start": 4.0, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "vice president in charge of national", "start": 8.16, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "defense and security of the Republic of", "start": 10.32, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "Equatorial Gina. I request protocol to", "start": 13.12, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "escort his excellency and invite him to", "start": 16.8, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "address the assembly.", "start": 20.08, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "Seenor Khalil Raman Mr. Khaled Rahman", "start": 41.36, "duration": 9.32}, {"text": "President of the General Assembly", "start": 46.8, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "Mr. Antonio Gutes,", "start": 50.879, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "Secretary General of the United Nations,", "start": 53.68, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "excellencies,", "start": 57.52, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "heads of state and government and heads", "start": 59.44, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "of delegation,", "start": 61.92, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "ladies and gentlemen,", "start": 63.68, "duration": 3.64}, {"text": "I have the honor to take the floor", "start": 67.92, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "before this general assembly", "start": 70.479, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "on behalf of and representing his", "start": 72.88, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "excellency Obang Gma Basogo, President", "start": 75.439, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "of the Republic of Equatorial Guinea.", "start": 78.32, "duration": 7.68}, {"text": "to express to you his greetings of peace", "start": 81.6, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "and the greetings of the people of", "start": 86.0, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "Equatorial Guinea and to reaffirm our", "start": 87.92, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "support for and commitment to the", "start": 92.0, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "charter of the United Nations.", "start": 93.84, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "I congratulate Mr.", "start": 99.28, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Rahman on his election", "start": 101.119, "duration": 8.32}, {"text": "to the presidency of this 81st session", "start": 104.88, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "and I express our gratitude", "start": 109.439, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "to Miss Analena Berbok", "start": 112.88, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "for her work during the previous", "start": 116.799, "duration": 7.481}, {"text": "session. Mr. President.", "start": 119.52, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "The theme of this session", "start": 124.64, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "is restoring trust, managing", "start": 128.319, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "transformation,", "start": 130.879, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "a united nations that delivers for all.", "start": 133.44, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "This theme invites us to consider", "start": 136.72, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "international cooperation", "start": 140.08, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "in a world that is subject to profound", "start": 142.239, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "challenges. for Equatorial Guinea.", "start": 144.56, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "Trust is strengthened", "start": 148.64, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "when we fulfill commitments that have", "start": 151.68, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "been made and decisions that have been", "start": 154.16, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "adopted collectively and when visible", "start": 156.08, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "results can be produced.", "start": 158.72, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "The countries of the global south", "start": 162.4, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "need cooperation that preserves peace,", "start": 165.12, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "that drives sustainable and inclusive", "start": 169.2, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "growth,", "start": 171.84, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "and that expands the ability of each", "start": 173.92, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "state to build its own future.", "start": 176.879, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "Therefore,", "start": 181.2, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "21st century cooperation", "start": 183.519, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "should provide opportunities for the", "start": 186.8, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "mobilization of financing", "start": 188.8, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "to transform transform raw materials and", "start": 191.28, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "to develop one's own knowledge and", "start": 195.12, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "technologies.", "start": 197.599, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "Excellencies,", "start": 199.28, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "this vision is especially relevant for", "start": 201.36, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "Africa, which needs investments that can", "start": 203.599, "duration": 8.081}, {"text": "allow it to develop local value chains.", "start": 207.36, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "Build infrastructure,", "start": 211.68, "duration": 6.68}, {"text": "advance industrialization,", "start": 214.879, "duration": 3.481}, {"text": ">> strengthen human capital,", "start": 218.4, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "incorporate new technologies, and", "start": 221.92, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "generate employment,", "start": 224.879, "duration": 3.481}, {"text": "especially for the continent's large", "start": 228.799, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "youth population.", "start": 231.84, "duration": 3.399}, {"text": "A more productive and industrialized", "start": 236.64, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "Africa will be a stronger partner for", "start": 239.599, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "all of the to benefit to the benefit of", "start": 243.36, "duration": 3.519}, {"text": "all of those wanting to halt its", "start": 245.36, "duration": 4.519}, {"text": "immigration.", "start": 246.879, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Excellencies,", "start": 250.72, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "when the 2030 agenda was adopted, the", "start": 252.799, "duration": 8.321}, {"text": "world embraced its deeply human vision,", "start": 256.32, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "eradicating poverty,", "start": 261.12, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "protecting the planet", "start": 263.52, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "and making sure that all people can live", "start": 267.199, "duration": 7.321}, {"text": "with dignity, leaving no one behind.", "start": 269.36, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "However, as we approach", "start": 276.24, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "its end date, we are far from meeting", "start": 279.68, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "its goals.", "start": 282.96, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Poverty persists,", "start": 286.16, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "inequality is expanding,", "start": 288.56, "duration": 7.4}, {"text": "and climate change continues to rage.", "start": 291.12, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "It is clear that we need an", "start": 296.16, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "international financial architecture", "start": 298.16, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "that facilitates productive investments", "start": 300.8, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "that takes into account vulner the real", "start": 303.759, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "vulnerabilities of developing countries", "start": 306.56, "duration": 8.76}, {"text": "and supports the efforts of each nation.", "start": 310.479, "duration": 4.841}, {"text": "It is therefore urgent to implement the", "start": 315.68, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "resolutions adopted at the conferences", "start": 318.56, "duration": 8.8}, {"text": "in Adesa in 2015 and in Sabia last year.", "start": 320.4, "duration": 10.28}, {"text": "Mr. President", "start": 327.36, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "development requires peace and", "start": 331.039, "duration": 4.921}, {"text": "stability.", "start": 332.96, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Ecuadoral Guinea defends dialogue,", "start": 336.32, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "negotiation,", "start": 339.84, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "mediation,", "start": 341.919, "duration": 7.241}, {"text": "and the peaceful settlement of disputes.", "start": 344.72, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "Our own experience demonstrates this.", "start": 349.84, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "Equatorial Guinea and the Gabanese", "start": 354.0, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "Republic", "start": 356.16, "duration": 2.8}, {"text": "are a clear example", "start": 359.199, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "of commitment to peaceful settlement", "start": 361.84, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "because they submitted their territorial", "start": 365.919, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "disputes to the International Court of", "start": 368.8, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Justice. Today, both states continue to", "start": 370.639, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "make progress on implementation through", "start": 374.4, "duration": 6.359}, {"text": "bilateral dialogue.", "start": 377.12, "duration": 3.639}, {"text": "We express our recognition and gratitude", "start": 385.44, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "for the valuable support of the United", "start": 388.639, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Nations and the African Union in this in", "start": 391.12, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "that process in which we have shown that", "start": 393.199, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "it is possible to preserve ties of", "start": 397.039, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "friendship, cooperation, and good", "start": 400.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "neighborliness. At the same time,", "start": 401.919, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "Equatorial Guinea has its doors wide", "start": 404.56, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "open for uh investors and partners from", "start": 407.28, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "around the world. We are an African", "start": 410.639, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "country in which you will find", "start": 413.44, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "stability,", "start": 415.919, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "tax advantages, opportunities,", "start": 417.84, "duration": 8.079}, {"text": "and a partner that is prepared to build", "start": 421.44, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "relationships of mutual benefit and", "start": 425.919, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "shared profit.", "start": 428.0, "duration": 3.319}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 432.24, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "distinguished delegations,", "start": 434.319, "duration": 3.561}, {"text": "restoring trust means showing that", "start": 440.16, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "working together produces results and", "start": 443.36, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "managing transformation means turning", "start": 446.319, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "the challenges of our time into new", "start": 449.199, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "opportunities.", "start": 451.599, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Africa brings together 54 United Nations", "start": 454.639, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "member states and represents a", "start": 457.44, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "fundamental share of the political and", "start": 460.88, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "demographic reality of the 21st century.", "start": 463.919, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "We must move towards a more balanced", "start": 468.24, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "international community in which Africa", "start": 470.88, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "participates fully in global decisions", "start": 473.68, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "and strengthens its ability to lead its", "start": 476.96, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "own development.", "start": 480.8, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "Equatorial", "start": 483.039, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Guinea reaffirms the African common", "start": 484.56, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "position as enshrined in the Ezelwini", "start": 487.599, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "consensus and the seat declaration", "start": 490.4, "duration": 8.4}, {"text": "which calls for two permanent seats with", "start": 495.199, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "veto right for Africa as well as two", "start": 498.8, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "additional non-permanent seats on the", "start": 501.759, "duration": 5.321}, {"text": "security council.", "start": 503.68, "duration": 3.4}, {"text": ">> Mr. President, excellencies, ladies and", "start": 510.24, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "gentlemen,", "start": 512.32, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "respect for international law, sovereign", "start": 514.8, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "equality, and friendship with all", "start": 517.839, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "peoples is what guides Equatorial", "start": 520.0, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "Guiney's foreign policy.", "start": 523.12, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Based on that position, we encourage the", "start": 526.0, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "United States of America and the", "start": 528.48, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "Republic of Cuba to continue to pursue", "start": 530.64, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "paths of dialogue which will make it", "start": 534.399, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "possible to end the blockade and build a", "start": 536.959, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "relationship of mutual benefit.", "start": 540.16, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "Moreover,", "start": 544.399, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "we see the United Nations as a universal", "start": 546.8, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "space for pursuing solutions to shared", "start": 549.36, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "problems.", "start": 552.24, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Equatorial Guinea maintains its trust in", "start": 554.399, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "this organization", "start": 556.88, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "because cooperation among nations", "start": 558.8, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "remains the most certain path towards", "start": 561.76, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "preserving peace and building shared", "start": 564.959, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "prosperity.", "start": 567.839, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "We also thank Mr. Antonio Guteres for", "start": 572.399, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "his years of service as Secretary", "start": 575.44, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "General,", "start": 577.44, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "for his commitment to peace and to the", "start": 579.2, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "attention he has paid to Africa.", "start": 582.32, "duration": 6.639}, {"text": "On behalf of President Obango,", "start": 585.6, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "the government and the people of", "start": 588.959, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "Equatorial Guinea, we express our", "start": 590.32, "duration": 7.48}, {"text": "gratitude to him. Excellencies,", "start": 592.959, "duration": 4.841}, {"text": "I will conclude by saying that the", "start": 597.92, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "history of the United Nations shows that", "start": 599.68, "duration": 7.279}, {"text": "peace and prosperity can move ahead when", "start": 602.8, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "nations work together.", "start": 606.959, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "And it is in that regard", "start": 610.0, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "that Equatorial Guinea will continue to", "start": 612.959, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "contribute based on mutual respect,", "start": 616.079, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "sovereign equality, and dialogue to turn", "start": 618.64, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "our cooperation into development and", "start": 621.04, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "opportunities for future generations.", "start": 624.16, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "Thank you very much.", "start": 626.0, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "On behalf", "start": 633.2, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "on behalf of the assembly, I wish to", "start": 635.839, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "thank the vice president in charge of", "start": 638.399, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "national defense and security of the", "start": 641.04, "duration": 6.68}, {"text": "equatorial ginia.", "start": 644.0, "duration": 3.72}]